{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-311a-7113-b4bf-7612516b7572"},"sequence":30,"recorded_at":1780531400000055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6e3c98747090b36dda943b643d","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-2f5393, status=development)' 2>&1; echo EXIT:$?\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2f5393/TASK-260830-2f5393_producer.md 2>&1\\necho ---BOARD---\\nTASK_BOARD_DIR=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board task-board m 'get_task(TASK-260830-2f5393)' 2>&1 | head -n 200\",\n  \"description\": \"Set status and read producer brief\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-2f5393\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"development\\\"}}}\\nEXIT:0\\nOwn TASK-260830-2f5393 (implement-lease-record-validation-and-cas), first leaf of STORY-260830-1oqfec (ownership-leases-and-fencing; siblings 3g12yp provider/pane fencing gates and 2atgj4 ownership reducer property tests follow you). Implement the Lease Record 1.0.0 lifecycle as production code: lease creation from the durable bootstrap inputs, renewal, expiry policy, epoch monotonicity, holder identity (host/process binding), and compare-and-swap writes over the durable record with the exact refusal classes the pinned sections 2.2, 5.3 and 13.6-13.10 name; the canonical Lease Record identity, winning-lease admission and fencing-token semantics that internal/sessquery and internal/sessstate already consume must be satisfied by what you write (do not fork a second lease model — extend internal/sessrepo lease.go or add a sibling package that sessquery's winningLeaseFor can adopt without behavioral change), including the crash/idempotency evidence for every durable mutation (real child-process termination at the rename seam, restart recovery, CAS conflict refusal, stale-epoch refusal, expired-lease refusal, holder mismatch refusal). Replace the task's v0.5.0 scope citations with the pinned v0.6.0 headings of the same sections. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on branch task-board/story/<STORY-ID> forked from the current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if git fetch origin shows that origin/main moved past the workspace base before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2f5393 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate source, test, harness and documentation paths (no task-board.config.json, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plant files; run Python harnesses with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract: every AC sentence and every gate/refusal is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test or declared a stated bound, reported as a ratio (n of m rows driven, call site named); negatives that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; at least one NARROWING mutant per gate (a token-preserving one where a gate inspects text) executed by a shipped harness on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, subprocess return-code exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; crash/idempotency evidence with real process termination where the operation mutates durable state; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to its owner/test; LOGBOOK.md and internal TRACEABILITY.md updated without unsupported claims; no CLI or unsupported capability advertised. Authority: pinned relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6 (internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json, embedded internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md) — the section numbers in the task scope refer to the retained headings of that revision; keep historical v0.5.0 (28bf96d) behavior compatible. Reuse the landed shared owners instead of duplicating them: internal/sessrepo (repository, event chain, lease and checkpoint record attestation), internal/sessstate (state reducer), internal/sessquery (selector, plans, winning-lease admission, sealed checkpoint admission), internal/canonicaljson (closed shapes), internal/localstore (paths, projection), internal/provhost (provider identity, manifest, probe, spawn, quiesce), internal/catalog and internal/traceability (contract census; run go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck and the cataloggen -check command from task-board.config.json). Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local, never hosted; run the affected packages while iterating and the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime constructs the Change Request with a 26-command suite after your handoff — hand off no later than 3 hours in; if the scope is not finished by then, hand off a coherent partial with the ratio stated honestly rather than exceeding the budget. Attach TASK-260830-2f5393_results.md, TASK-260830-2f5393_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2f5393_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-2f5393 --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: codex gpt-5.6-luna max (operator fallback while Muse Spark transport is failing). The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n---BOARD---\\nmutation error: parse error at 1:1: unknown operation \\\"get_task\\\" (got \\\"get_task\\\"); known operations: accept_cr, add_checklist_item, add_resource, assign, audit_context_validation, check_item, collect_context_retention, confirm_context_reclamation, correct_activity, create, defer_cr, delete, delete_resource, handoff, integrate_external, link, login, logout, mark_context_stale, normalize_legacy_status, publish_context, reclassify_context, record_ledger_event, register_context, remove_checklist_item, rename, retire_context, retry_context_payload_withdrawal, set_details, set_estimate, set_notes, set_parent, set_status, sweep_context_retention, sweep_context_validation_audits, switch_user, unassign, uncheck_item, undefer_cr, unlink, update_resource, withdraw_cr; see schema() for the contract and schema(mutation=NAME) for one signature\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5841,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1461,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
