{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-311a-7113-b4bf-7612516b7572"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6e-9a14-7171-bdba-897a8c5d81d7"},"task_id":"01a0ad6e-9a14-7171-bdba-897a8c5d81d7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6e-9a14-7171-bdba-897a8c5d81d7","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-6-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"^## 2\\\\.2\\\\|^## 5\\\\.3\\\\|^## 13\\\\.6\\\\|^## 13\\\\.7\\\\|^## 13\\\\.8\\\\|^## 13\\\\.9\\\\|^## 13\\\\.10\\\\|^### 2\\\\.2\\\\|^### 5\\\\.3\\\\|^### 13\\\\.\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 30; echo ===; grep -n \\\"2\\\\.2\\\\|Lease\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate spec section headings\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"404:### 2.2 Global invariants\\n1908:### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\\n8993:### 13.1 Direct-session launch\\n9095:### 13.2 Task-board session launch\\n9168:### 13.3 Sync\\n9212:### 13.4 Local attach\\n9224:### 13.5 Remote attach\\n9253:### 13.6 Graceful takeover\\n9363:### 13.7 Force takeover\\n9533:### 13.8 Fork\\n9802:### 13.9 Stop\\n9852:### 13.10 Resume\\n9918:### 13.11 Reboot restore\\n9943:### 13.12 Failure and recovery matrix\\n9967:### 13.13 Crash/restart outcome gate\\n10041:### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\\n10985:### 13.15 Directory continuation planning and execution\\n===\\n143:| Lease record | <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n208:allocates neither Configuration 4 nor RPC 5. Session Record, Event, Lease and\\n326:event order. Lease epochs, predecessor links, and deterministic conflict rules\\n383:| Lease | An immutable ownership grant containing an epoch, predecessor, holder, and fencing token. |\\n384:| Lease epoch | A monotonically increasing positive <code>uint53</code> counter scoped to one logical session. |\\n404:### 2.2 Global invariants\\n1908:### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\\n1910:The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\\n1915:| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\\n1917:| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\\n1920:| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\\n1956:order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\\n2952:| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\\n3142:| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\\n3143:| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, mate