{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dd8d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-311a-7113-b4bf-7612516b7572"},"sequence":3361,"recorded_at":1780531400006717,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"020be8ef-fb6e-418b-83cb-2187067ba7da"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260830-2f5393 (implement lease record validation and CAS) is complete: status `to-review`, checklist 14/14, three outcome resources attached and verified. Work is left uncommitted in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\n\nWhat was delivered, in `internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go` (~800 lines): epoch-1 `CreateLease` from durable bootstrap inputs, `CompareAndSwapLease` with expected-head compare (conflict vs stale classification plus crashed-commit replay that re-mints against the pre-commit basis), tuple-ordered readers, `VerifyFencingToken` renewal, and `CheckFencingExpiry` grant-expiry. Key spec decision: the lease itself never expires (pinned by an ancient-`created_at` test) — only the process-local fencing grant lapses. No second lease model: shape/identity stay with `canonicaljson`, the tuple rule stays with `sessstate.Compare` (agreement-pinned across the import cycle), and `winningLeaseFor` is unchanged (adoption test proves store-minted records admit there).\n\nEvidence: 8 of 8 AC rows driven through production entries by named tests; every one of the 26 new `refuse` sites carries a narrowing mutant (27/27 applied plants KILLED including the token-preserving timestamp mutant, exit 0, per-plant raw logs in the tarball); real SIGKILL child drills at the rename seam for create and CAS; refusal census at 61 sites and equality census at 3 ledgered sites, both green. Full suite, full race (26/26), coverage (sessrepo 86.6%), all 13 fuzz smokes, tracecheck, cataloggen, cross-compiles, and `task-board validate` (exit 0) pass. The provhost 5-site attestation bound holds without rewriting it — the mint confirm routes through `AttestLeaseRecord`.\n\nStated bounds: 0 of 8 rows as public CLI (no `ax` command in tree); checkpoint-record admission, takeover/fork orchestration, and cross-partition union convergence stay with their owning leaves.","reason":null}}
